# NexaGO Design System

## Product Philosophy

The platform is a tournament operating system focused on operational clarity, fast mobile use, and real-time readability in outdoor environments.

The UI should feel competitive, modern, energetic, and data-oriented. Avoid generic SaaS aesthetics that dilute the sports identity.

## Visual Direction

Use the Court System direction:

- dark surfaces on `--nx-surface-0` / `--nx-surface-1`
- orange accent on `--color-primary`
- subtle borders on `--nx-line`
- restrained elevation (`--nx-elev-1`, `--nx-elev-2`, `--nx-elev-3`)
- glass overlays via `--nx-glass-blur` and `--nx-glass-saturate`
- orange glow only for live or focused states (`--nx-glow-orange`)

Do not rely on heavy blur stacks, neon cyan/purple gradients, or oversized shadows in dark mode.

## Tokens

Prefer the `nx-*` tokens from `src/app/styles/tokens.scss`:

- spacing: `--nx-s-1` through `--nx-s-9`
- radius: `--nx-r-1` through `--nx-r-5`, `--nx-radius-pill`
- motion: `--nx-d-fast`, `--nx-d-base`, `--nx-d-slow`
- easing: `--nx-ease-out`, `--nx-ease-spring`
- labels: `--nx-font-label`

Legacy `--space-*` and `--radius-*` tokens remain for older screens; migrate new work to `nx-*`.

## Core Rules

- One full-orange primary CTA per screen.
- Secondary actions use ghost or solid-dark variants.
- Cards use 18px radius, 1px `--nx-line`, and light elevation by default.
- Text fields are 52px tall with visible uppercase labels.
- Primary buttons use white text on orange (`--color-on-primary`).
- Minimum touch target is 44x44px.
- Common UI transitions should stay at or below 240ms.
- Prefer skeleton shimmer over centered spinners for page loading.
- Skeletons appear after `--nx-skeleton-delay` (200ms) and use low-chroma shimmer for 1.4s.
- In-app toasts auto-dismiss after `--nx-toast-duration` (4s) with slide-down entry and swipe-up dismiss.

## Shared Components

Use the primitives in `src/app/components/shared/ui/` before inventing page-specific markup:

- `app-ui-button`
- `app-ui-card`
- `app-ui-input`
- `app-ui-chip`
- `app-ui-segmented-control`
- `app-ui-skeleton`
- `app-ui-avatar`
- `app-ui-list-row`
- `app-ui-bottom-sheet`
- `app-ui-live-scoreboard`
- `app-ui-toast`
- `app-ui-empty-state`
- `app-ui-loading-state`

Domain-aligned surfaces:

- `app-match-card` (scheduled / live / final variants, set ribbon, live glow)
- `app-mobile-nav-footer` (floating tab bar, 64px, glass blur)
- `app-navbar` (Top Bar 64px, root/detail modes)
- `app-toast-container` (in-app toast stack)

### Match Card

- Estados visuais: `scheduled` (meta `#N · QUADRA`, chip com horário, placar `—`), `live` (meta `SET n · mm:ss`, chip `AO VIVO`, glow laranja, ribbon mono dos sets encerrados), `final` (meta fase + quadra, chip `ENCERRADA`, sets vencidos com vencedor em verde, ribbon `21-18` por set).
- Toque curto emite `cardOpen`; long-press ou botão “Mais ações” abre `app-ui-bottom-sheet` com `quickActions` e conteúdo projetado em `[data-match-card-actions]`.
- `options.interactive: false` desativa gestos; `options.showContextFooter` controla rodapés contextuais (bracket, atleta, vitória/derrota).

### Toast

- Variants: info (orange), success (green), error (live red).
- Sports notifications should lead with compact pair/score title when data is available.
- Tap navigates when `action.route` is provided.

### Empty State

- Geometric icon at 64px, title 18px bold, subtitle 13px muted.
- Optional CTA via `app-ui-button` (primary uses white on orange).

### Skeleton

- Presets: `block`, `circle`, `matchCard`, `listRow`, `pageHeader`, `bracketTree`.
- Do not use centered page spinners; match the loading layout shape.

Global utility classes in `src/styles.scss` such as `.nx-card`, `.nx-btn`, `.nx-input`, `.nx-auth-*`, `.nx-chip`, `.nx-segmented`, and `.nx-skeleton` should stay aligned with those components.

## Auth Screens

Login and register should use the auth shell/card pattern:

- Google action: ghost
- form submit: primary
- register submit: primary `lg`
